# 1Password value resolution for directorate-of-equality-api — LOCAL DEVELOPMENT ONLY.
#
# See config/1password/README.md for the model, the caching note, how to migrate
# an app, and why decorator names must not appear in prose in this file.

# @defaultRequired=infer
# @plugin(@varlock/1password-plugin)
# @initOp(token=$OP_TOKEN, allowAppAuth=true)
# @setValuesBulk(opLoadEnvironment($OP_SHARED_ENVIRONMENT))
# @setValuesBulk(opLoadEnvironment($OP_APP_ENVIRONMENT))
# @import(../../../apps/directorate-of-equality-api/)
# ---

# Scoped, read-only 1Password service account token, held in the macOS Keychain
# rather than in a file or the shell.
#
# Without it this falls back to desktop-app authentication, which authorises PER
# RUN -- a prompt on every `nx serve`. Desktop auth also connects as the
# developer, with their full vault access, where the service account is limited
# to the environments it actually needs. keychain() still authenticates, but per
# SESSION rather than per run.
#
# The Keychain account name is pinned rather than defaulted. varlock derives the
# default from the current directory name, so it differs between the main
# checkout and each worktree, and a ref written in one tree would not resolve in
# another. Recreate the item with:
#
#   varlock keychain set        OP_TOKEN --account dmr.is:local:OP_TOKEN
#   varlock keychain fix-access          --account dmr.is:local:OP_TOKEN
#
# fix-access is not optional. Without it macOS asks for the login password on
# every read instead of letting varlock's helper through -- which is worse than
# the prompt this replaces.
#
# The service account needs read access to EVERY environment it resolves: the
# shared one plus each app's. Missing that, resolution fails at the first
# setValuesBulk line with a generic "an unexpected error occurred while
# processing the request", which looks nothing like a permissions problem and
# cost an afternoon.
#
# allowAppAuth stays true above. The token takes precedence when present, so
# this only means anyone without the Keychain item keeps working through the
# desktop app rather than failing outright.
# @type=opServiceAccountToken @internal
OP_TOKEN=keychain("varlock", account="dmr.is:local:OP_TOKEN")

# Holds only keys that are either byte-identical across every deployed service
# (IDENTITY_SERVER_DOMAIN, the four NATIONAL_REGISTRY_*, XROAD_DMR_CLIENT,
# XROAD_ISLAND_IS_PATH) or absent from every deployment and the same on every
# laptop (LOCAL_CHROMIUM_PATH). Nothing else. Keep it disjoint from the app environment
# below -- which of the two wins for a duplicated key is still unverified, so a
# key must live in exactly one of them.
# @public @internal
OP_SHARED_ENVIRONMENT=xg6t32oousqpfj5lbmj4gpjxqe

# Everything this app needs, named as its ECS task definition names it.
# @public @internal
OP_APP_ENVIRONMENT=4zzzpkis7f25sl5flpoywbjhtq
